while on a rare trip president vladimir  putin sang the russian anthem with  students and held an open class on the  first day of school  he talked with the children about  fighting in ukraine and visited a naval  institute  putin was in kaliningrad a chunk of  russia on the baltic sea surrounded by  nato countries for putin this little  slice of territory is really important  because it gives him a point  from which he can pressure europe  the region has been at the center of  tensions amid the ukraine war with  russia deploying more military forces  and the transit of goods being disrupted  here's why kaliningrad is so important  for the kremlin  as this map shows kalinigrad is  sandwiched between poland and lithuania  both of which are in the eu and are part  of nato  the former german territory was given to  moscow as a result of world war ii and  it was disconnected from the rest of the  russian mainland by the breakup of the  soviet union  the region is strategically important as  it provides an exit onto the baltic sea  where russia has a big naval fleet as  nato supports ukraine in its fight  against russia's invasion the outpost  has been of growing concern for the west  putin has this jumping off point from  which he can sort of threaten european  and nato members before the invasion of  ukraine moscow deployed nuclear-capable  missiles in kaliningrad following the  invasion the military build-up continued  in august russia said it had sent  warplanes armed with hypersonic missiles  to the region it's essentially russia  reminding the west what it's capable of  and where it has a strategic outpost in  europe  in june anxiety in the region increased  after neighboring lithuania banned the  rail transfer of some goods between  kaliningrad and continental russia  through its territory angering moscow  the region is a manufacturing hub that  imports and exports materials including  concrete wood and industrial chemicals  to the mainland  lithuania has said it was implementing  eu sanctions on russia but moscow called  the move unlawful and warned lithuanians  of serious consequences  tensions were diffused at least  temporarily after other european nations  urged vilnius not to inflame the  situation  they came up with a quota um and so  russia is still allowed to send goods  but every so often we've heard some  quibbles from moscow still that not  enough is getting through  military analysts say the risk of an  actual armed confrontation between nato  and russia in the region is currently  limited  instead putin's visit highlights how  important kaliningrad is for moscow as  the territory is increasingly isolated  in the region what political analysts  believe is by taking this trip putin is  essentially sending a message to europe  he's saying clinton grad is here and  don't mess with it
 

